Hi,
I thought that my first ascension as a valkyrie would stop me from playing
this game but it's like a drug. Actually I don't want to tell about this one,
but about my second ascension as an archaeologist because in the first I used
some "illegal" tricks like savegame-copy and when something happened I didn't
like, I just quit and restored the old copy. But since I'm not able to rebuild
collapsed dungeons, I still do this but, honestly, only for that reason.
I'm playing NetHack 3.1.2 on my PC at home (BTW, are there major differences
to version 3.1.3?)

First my final stats:
St: 25, Dx: 18, Co: 18, In: 22, Wi: 22, Ch: 11
Hp 350 (350), Pw: 400 (400), AC -57
I ascended with about 3.8 million points after about 52000 moves.

Now to the game: (maybe some spoilers)
^L













I was very lucky to get Grayswandir on dlvl 3 by offering a gecko. With this,
the gnomish mines were no problem. Later I robbed all the vaults with my
pick-axe and found a temple on dlvl 20 where I got my AC lowered. Then I went
to Fort Ludios and returned to the priestess with all the gold. Altogether she
got 88000 zorkmids and my AC was -11. Meanwhile I was ready for the quest and
was lucky to have a savegame-copy when on the lowest quest-level the dungeon
collapsed. But anyway, the quest itself was quite easy (snakes and mummies)
and I had intrinsic "searching". With 2 blessed magig lamps I wished for speed
boots and GDSM. The third one I kept 'til the end. In the castle I wished for
a blessed figurine of an Archon (nicest pet IMO and you get a SoR) and I went
with it to the endgame. No wonder that you can't polymorph into one. On the
first gehennom level it killed all the wraithes and I was level 30. Then I
just went through gehennom only picking up some wands of digging, found a
scroll of genocide on a bones pile and summoned some more wraithes. At this
moment my armor and weapon were already quite perfect:
 +4 GDSM, +6 CoP, +5 speed boots, +4 GoP, +4 SoR, +4HoB, +4 Ring of Prot. and
 +5 Grayswandir = AC -57 all blessed and rustproof/fireproof.
With this equipment, the rest of the game was quite easy.

What I did else:
- genocided all L's (for me) and purple worms (for my pet)
- second wish from the wand: WoD
- charged my WoW with a scroll (luck for me that it worked)
- wished for charging scroll
- charged my magic marker
- wrote some blessed charging scrolls (couldn't charge the mm with these)
- kept some potions of (extra) healing to throw on my pet when nescessary

During the game I found a lot of spellbooks (~30) and due to high In. and Wi.
I could read and use them all. Especially in gehennom I like it to do magic
mapping and detect treasure when entering a new level and then just run or
teleport through. So finally I arrived at he wizard's tower, killed him, got
the book, went down, and I think after 2000 moves I found the vibrating square
since an umber hulk pet, which I had at this time messed up the whole level.
On my way back with the Amulet I noticed several black glows and malignant
auras but luckily my BoH remained blessed. All together I killed the Wizard
10-15 times either with WoD, cockatrice corpse or just with Grayswandir. The
endgame was rather easy too, since at this time I already had 350 HP and it
never went below 250. On the Astral Plane I just used my WoTel. to get rid of
these demons and on the second altar I could offer the Amulet. That's it.

But I have one question left:
What the hell is the difference between my quest artifact "Orb of detection"
and an ordinary crystal ball??? I tried to invoke its power several times and
the game always told me something like: "You feel a surge of power, but
nothing happens."
